Z||000014||Denny||12-28-2001||09:26 PM||||We've owned 4   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and killed one of those   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">.<P>Wonder if those numbers are fairly typical?<P>Also have friends who have parted 3 Fieros since I've known them, and they still own 3.<P>Another family I know has 13 (maybe 14 now), only one of which is not being actively resurrected.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Denny (edited 12-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Archie||12-29-2001||12:40 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FIERO JOHN-WI:<BR><B> Plus Hope to see all of you at the 11th Annual Midwest Fiero Dells Run. More info about the Dells Run 2002 will be posted in January, infact so much you'll have to attend just to find out, why everyone is talking about it!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree with John. Anyone who has ever attended the Dells show will be able to tell you that THIS is truely the National show (or should be).<P>This is the premiere Fiero Show. It has everything that everyone dreams about in the ideal show. <P>The Accommodations: The show takes place at a fine Resort in the Dells, they have lots of very nice rooms and everything you want in a resort. The Mid-West Clubs all have events Dinners, cruises, tours & other events you can also go karting, go play Golf right next door etc. A person can Could spend the entire long weekend with activities without even leaving the Resort. Last year after the show was over, my wife and I stayed for another 4 days.<P>The Organization: The people who put this event (it's not just a show) on every year put on the best show all the time. You'll never hear anyone bitching them out because of lack of organization. You won't have to worry about hearing all kinds of excuses because of poor planning. The events and get togethers go off on time and exactly as planned. <P>The Show: What can I say, John is usually the guy that gets the cars parked in the right places for the show & he's a master of it. AND it goes off on schedule. During the show, you can listen to the music put on by the D.J. and announcements are made through out the show for door prises. I only wish the show could last for 2 days so that I could visit with everyone. When the car show is over they are just as well organized getting the cars out of the show area. This event is called the Dells Cruise and right at the end of the car show John and the rest of them line up the show cars and take them on a cruise thru the Dells area for all to see.<P>My wife and I have gone to this show every year for the last 5 years. This is the PERFECT SHOW for the Fiero owner with a family. My wife is not a "car Show" type person, but she always likes going to this show. There are all kinds of things for the wife and kids to do besides Fieros. Dinners, Tours, outings with other members, super nice rooms, room service, in room movies. She's a happy camper and I get to do Fieros.<P>The Perfect Weekend.<P>IMHO, if you are only able to attend one show per year, this should be the one.<P>Archie<P>------------------<BR>Just how fast do you want to go?||||reg||1
